Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an inconsistency in the byte order of the GUID structure, where some components were stored in little-endian format while others were in big-endian format. This mismatch led to incorrect comparisons and representations of GUIDs, as the EFI specification requires a specific byte order that was not being adhered to in the original implementation.

